      "content": "Certainly. The specific technical risks involving the Authentication (Auth) module were as follows:\n\n1. Timestamp Synchronization: There were discrepancies found in clock synchronization across different environments, which might affect JWT token generation. We're tasked with a final check and ensuring time is accurately synced before we go live.\n\n2. Rate Limiting Parameters: The Auth module's rate limiting thresholds are lower for beta testers than needed for production, risk of service outages during high usage has been observed in our previous beta test. We're adjusting those parameters and doubling testing to ensure they're set optimally.\n\n3. Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) Bugs: Minor bugs were discovered during testing related to the MFA implementation, mainly with older authentication libraries. We're on track to apply the necessary patches by end of today.\n\nRest assured, our QA team has prioritized these issues and the final push will include an additional full-system load test to guarantee that everything is fully operational and stable when we go live.",
